  <page_number>278</page_number>
  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>bo-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">tamen deficiat, ipsa pars affecta,</l>
    <l n="2">sibimet profpicit. Ita &amp; si ma-</l>
    <l n="3">gistratus malo remedium non</l>
    <l n="4">paret, singulis saltem id sibi</l>
    <l n="5">parare permittetur.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Verùm respondeo, hæc qui-</l>
    <l n="7">dem speciosa videri, non ta-</l>
    <l n="8">men admittenda esse. Et quod</l>
    <l n="9">tales ponantur casus, qui non[?]</l>
    <l n="10">evenient, ut scilicet judices sint</l>
    <l n="11">denegaturi justitiam. Et si forte</l>
    <l n="12">evenirent, præstaret patienter</l>
    <l n="13">injurias ferre, quam ut nosmet</l>
    <l n="14">ipsos vindicaremus. Præsertim</l>
    <l n="15">cum inter verbalem illam in-</l>
    <l n="16">juriam &amp; vitam hominis inju-</l>
    <l n="17">riantis non sit proportio. Et</l>
    <l n="18">plus injurianti adimeretur,</l>
    <l n="19">quia vita, quam nobis, quibus</l>
    <l n="20">aliquid tantum, vana quo-</l>
    <l n="21">rundam opinione, non in rei</l>
    <l n="22">veritate ademptum esset. Ut</l>
    <l n="23">omnes illæ regulæ, &amp; axioma-</l>
    <l n="24">ta allegata, potissimum locum</l>
    <l n="25">habeant, in casubus, ubi agitur</l>
    <l n="26">de corporis adeoque vitæ, &amp;</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The word "non" after "qui" has a dark mark over it in the scan, so I have marked it [?]. The "s" forms are long s in the print and are written as plain s. "Verùm" keeps its printed grave accent. The catchword "bo-" is at the foot and is not repeated in the text.</notes>
</page>
